# APML v2.0.0 - Driving Mode (Background Audio Playback)
# SSI Learning App
# Last Updated: 2026-06-08

spec driving_mode:
  version: "2.0.0"
  status: "superseded — goal achieved a different way; the concatenator design was never built"
  date: "2026-06-08"

  description: |
    Background audio playback for hands-free learning while driving, walking, or
    doing other activities. Solves the iOS Safari limitation around backgrounded /
    locked playback.

    Core insight (still true): SSi is radio, not Duolingo. The screen is theater
    for the sale; the ears do the work. Users MUST be able to learn while looking
    at their satnav.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## STATUS: WHAT ACTUALLY SHIPPED (2026-06-08)
  ## ==========================================================================

  reality:
    summary: |
      The "concatenate each round into one big WAV song" design in this spec was
      NEVER built, and its files were deleted. None of these exist:
        - packages/player-vue/src/composables/useDrivingMode.ts        (never created)
        - packages/player-vue/src/components/DrivingModeToggle.vue      (never created)
        - packages/player-vue/src/utils/audioConcatenator.ts           (DELETED, commit 59a17a7b^)
        - packages/player-vue/src/utils/silentAudio.ts                 (DELETED — the LOOPED-silence landmine)
        - packages/player-vue/src/playback/SessionController.ts        (DELETED — whole playback island gone)

      There is no separate "Driving Mode" toggle. Instead the SAME normal player
      now plays correctly while backgrounded / on the lock screen, so the
      hands-free goal is met without a distinct mode. The live mechanism is three
      independent pieces (NOT round concatenation, NOT the silent-placeholder
      LOOP trick this spec described):

      1. Media Session API — lock-screen + car-bluetooth metadata and controls.
         setupMediaSession() / clearMediaSession() in
         packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue (~line 4744),
         wired to the live SimplePlayer (resume/pause/skipRound/jumpToRound).
         A parallel copy lives in ListeningOverlay.vue for pod playback.

      2. AudioContext silent-oscillator keepalive — holds the iOS audio session
         alive across PAUSE phases and inter-clip gaps. Sits UNDERNEATH the
         <audio> element (never on it). composables/useAudioSessionKeepalive.ts.
         Per CLAUDE.md this is verified ~30+ min locked; field notes dispute
         sufficiency for true screen-off lock (see buffer-model.md open question).

      3. Silent one-shot pause clip — during PAUSE, SimplePlayer plays a
         genuinely-silent real-PCM WAV (buildSilentWavDataUri, playback/silentWav.ts)
         on the SAME element the cycle uses, so PAUSE advances on the audio
         element's natural 'ended' (a clock iOS does not throttle when locked)
         instead of a backgrounded setTimeout. STRICTLY one-shot — never looped
         (looping is the disabled 2026-05-23 oscillation landmine, and is exactly
         what the old silentAudio.ts "driving mode" did wrong).

    do_not_reintroduce: |
      NEVER add silent audio ON or ALONGSIDE the main <audio> element to "keep it
      alive" (no silent-WAV LOOP, no playSilentKeepalive, no second <audio>). The
      tell is the lock widget flickering play/pause and playback dying after ~1
      cycle even fully cached. Re-introduced and reverted twice. The round-concat
      "song" + looped silent-placeholder design below is the abandoned approach;
      it is kept only as design archaeology. Keepalive (Web Audio, below the
      element) and supply (the buffer) are orthogonal and must never be conflated.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## OFFLINE SUPPLY (LIVE) — how hands-free audio stays fed without network
  ## ==========================================================================

  offline_supply:
    summary: |
      "Driving mode" needs audio to keep arriving with no network. That is the
      buffer/cache layer, NOT a separate mode. One system: online just fills the
      same cache from the network instead of from a pre-download; the player only
      ever reads from the cache. See docs/buffer-model.md + docs/cold-start-and-playback.md.

    one_system:
      cachePlayOnline: |
        const cachePlayOnline (LearningPlayer.vue) defaults ON — online playback
        reads WAV blobs decoded from cached MP3s (createAudioCacheSource →
        AudioCache.getWavBlobUrl), exactly like offline. ?stream bypasses it.
      rolling_filler: |
        LearningPlayer's rolling FILLER (fillBuffer/expandScript, ROLLING_SPAN_MS
        ~20 min) walks forward from the cursor collecting unique /api/audio ids
        and lands them via audioCache.persistent.ensure (IndexedDB). Plus
        SimplePlayer.prefetchNextCycle warms the next cycle, and the SW caches the
        app shell only — the SW is NOT in the audio path.
      blob_play_caveat: |
        WebKit won't play a blob: URL backed by mp3 bytes from IDB, so the offline
        resolve path decodes each cached MP3 → 16-bit WAV blob (cache/wav.ts). This
        is the surviving fragment of the deleted audioConcatenator.

    deliberate_download: |
      A user-initiated deep download exists and is LIVE (this is the closest thing
      to the spec's "download the course" idea — not parked, but depth-based not
      ms-based):
        - LearningPlayer.downloadForOffline() collects audio ids round-by-round
          (depth chosen as a % / span of the course) and calls
          audioCache.persistent.ensure on each.
        - Progress is shared via composables/useOfflineDownloadStatus.ts
          (offlineDlState idle|preparing|downloading|complete|error, done/total/failed)
          and drawn as a ring on the mode button + the Offline row in ModeTray
          (no floating banner).
      AudioCache namespaces: persistent (survives, used here) vs ephemeral
      (vestigial — kept for now, not the offline store).

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## ARCHIVED DESIGN (NOT BUILT) — the original concatenate-per-round proposal
  ## Everything below documents the abandoned approach. The iOS *problem* it
  ## frames is real and still solved; the *solution* it proposes (round
  ## concatenation + looped silent placeholder) was replaced by the three-piece
  ## mechanism in `reality:` above. Read for rationale, not as current code.
  ## ==========================================================================

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## THE iOS PROBLEM
  ## ==========================================================================

  ios_problem:
    issue: |
      iOS Safari blocks audio.src changes when the page is backgrounded.
      The Audio element that's playing continues, but starting NEW audio fails.
      This breaks atomic file playback where each phrase is a separate file.

    failed_approaches:
      - "Web Audio API - suspended when backgrounded"
      - "Multiple Audio elements - src change still blocked"
      - "Media Source Extensions - limited iOS support"
      - "Service Worker audio - no DOM/AudioContext access"

    solution: |
      1. Concatenate all audio for a round into a single file (audio sprite)
      2. Play single file - no src changes needed during round
      3. Use "silent audio placeholder" trick between rounds
      4. Media Session API provides lock screen and car controls

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SILENT AUDIO PLACEHOLDER TRICK
  ## ==========================================================================

  silent_audio_trick:
    purpose: "Keep iOS audio session alive between rounds"

    how_it_works: |
      iOS revokes audio permissions when playback STOPS.
      By playing silent audio just before the main track ends,
      the audio session never terminates, so the page retains
      playback privileges for the next track.

    implementation:
      timing: "Start silent audio ~1 second before main audio ends"
      file: "1 second of silence (generated via Web Audio API, ~2KB)"
      element: "Separate Audio element with loop=true"

    sequence:
      1: "mainAudio playing round N..."
      2: "timeRemaining < 1 second"
      3: "silentAudio.play() - keeps session alive"
      4: "mainAudio 'ended' event fires"
      5: "mainAudio.src = round N+1 blob URL"
      6: "mainAudio.play() - WORKS because session active"
      7: "silentAudio.pause()"
      8: "Repeat for next round"

    source: "Battle-tested by SoundWheel and other production audio apps"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## ROUND AS SONG METAPHOR
  ## ==========================================================================

  round_as_song:
    description: |
      Each round (~5 minutes, ~21 cycles) is treated as a single "song".
      Users see familiar music player controls on lock screen and car dashboard.

    user_experience:
      lock_screen:
        title: "Round 3 of 12"
        artist: "SSi Spanish"
        album: "Driving Mode"
        controls: ["previous", "play/pause", "next", "scrubber"]

      car_bluetooth:
        steering_wheel_buttons: "Skip to next/previous round"
        dashboard_display: "Basic metadata (varies by car)"
        carplay: "NOT SUPPORTED - requires native app"

    why_5_minutes: |
      ~21 cycles × ~12 seconds = ~4-5 minutes per round
      Long enough to be meaningful, short enough to feel like progress
      Natural break points for user-initiated skipping

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## AUDIO CONCATENATION
  ## ==========================================================================

  audio_concatenation:
    purpose: "Create single audio file per round for uninterrupted playback"
    status: "ARCHIVED — utils/audioConcatenator.ts DELETED (commit 59a17a7b^)"
    surviving_descendant: |
      The per-round concatenation was abandoned, but its decode-mp3-bytes →
      re-encode-16-bit-WAV core was lifted (minus concat/normalisation) into
      packages/player-vue/src/cache/wav.ts. That powers OFFLINE playback only:
      WebKit refuses to play a blob: URL backed by mp3 bytes from IndexedDB, but
      plays WAV blobs fine, so the offline resolve path decodes each cached MP3
      clip to a WAV blob (AudioCache.getWavBlobUrl via createAudioCacheSource).
      Online streaming hands the proxy /api/audio URL straight to the element.
    file: "(DELETED) packages/player-vue/src/utils/audioConcatenator.ts → see cache/wav.ts"

    process:
      1: "Fetch all audio files for round (via getAudioSource)"
      2: "Decode to AudioBuffers using AudioContext.decodeAudioData()"
      3: "Create silence buffers for PAUSE phases (4 seconds)"
      4: "Concatenate in cycle order: KNOWN → PAUSE → VOICE1 → VOICE2"
      5: "Add small gaps (200ms) between audio files"
      6: "Encode to WAV blob (16-bit PCM, 44.1kHz)"
      7: "Return blob URL + segment timestamps"

    output:
      blob: "WAV audio blob (~15MB for 5 minutes)"
      blobUrl: "Object URL for playback"
      segments: "Array of {id, phase, startTime, endTime, cycleIndex}"
      totalDuration: "Total length in seconds"

    performance:
      fetch_30_files: "200-500ms on mobile"
      decode: "500-1500ms on mobile"
      concatenate: "50-100ms"
      encode_wav: "100-200ms"
      total: "1-3 seconds on mobile"
      memory_peak: "~50MB during processing"

    why_wav_not_mp3: |
      - Simpler encoding (no lamejs dependency)
      - Reliable seeking (no VBR issues)
      - Size acceptable (~15MB for 5 min, temporary blob)
      - Faster encoding than MP3

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SEGMENT TRACKING
  ## ==========================================================================

  segment_tracking:
    purpose: "Map currentTime to cycle/phase for position tracking and resume"

    segment_structure:
      id: "Audio ID or generated ID for silence"
      phase: "'known' | 'pause' | 'voice1' | 'voice2'"
      startTime: "Seconds from start of concatenated audio"
      endTime: "Seconds from start of concatenated audio"
      cycleIndex: "0-based index of cycle within round"

    usage:
      during_playback: |
        Track mainAudio.currentTime
        Find segment where startTime <= currentTime < endTime
        Update Media Session metadata based on phase
        Notify position callbacks

      on_exit: |
        Map current segment to {roundIndex, cycleIndex, phase}
        Return position for normal mode resume
        (ARCHIVED) the deleted SessionController.jumpToPosition() did this.
        Live equivalent: SimplePlayer.jumpToRound(roundIndex, cycleIndex)
        in packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## CHAIN LOADING
  ## ==========================================================================

  chain_loading:
    purpose: "Seamless round-to-round transitions without upfront wait"

    strategy: |
      While playing round N, concatenate round N+1 in background.
      When round N ends, immediately switch to round N+1.
      Start concatenating round N+2.
      Repeat until session complete or user exits.

    state_machine:
      preparing: "Concatenating first round (user sees progress)"
      playing: "Playing current round"
      loading_next: "Playing AND concatenating next round"
      paused: "Playback paused by user"
      inactive: "Not in driving mode"

    memory_management: |
      Only keep current + next round in memory
      Call URL.revokeObjectURL() after switching rounds
      Peak memory: ~30MB (2 × 15MB blobs)

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## MEDIA SESSION API
  ## ==========================================================================

  media_session:
    purpose: "Lock screen and car bluetooth controls"
    status: "LIVE — this part DID ship (the only part of this spec that did)"
    file: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue (setupMediaSession ~L4744); pod copy in components/ListeningOverlay.vue"

    metadata_as_built:
      title: "'SSi Learning'  (static — NOT 'Round N of total')"
      artist: "'Practice Session'"
      album: "'Player'"
      note: "The dynamic per-round metadata below was the archived design and is not implemented."

    action_handlers_as_built:
      play: "if not playing → simplePlayer.resume()"
      pause: "if playing → simplePlayer.pause()"
      nexttrack: "simplePlayer.skipRound()"
      previoustrack: "if roundIndex>0 → simplePlayer.jumpToRound(idx-1)"
      not_wired: "seekbackward / seekforward / seekto / scrubber are NOT registered in the live player"
    playback_state: "watch(isPlaying) → navigator.mediaSession.playbackState = 'playing'|'paused'"

    archived_design_metadata:
      title: "Round {N} of {total}"
      artist: "SSi Learning"
      album: "Driving Mode"
      artwork: "Belt-colored icon (192px, 512px)"
      seek_handlers: "seekbackward 10s / seekforward 10s / seekto (scrubber)"

    position_state:
      duration: "Round total duration"
      playbackRate: "1.0"
      position: "Current time in round"
      update_frequency: "Every animation frame during playback"

    user_gesture_note: |
      Media Session action handlers ARE treated as user gestures on iOS
      (fixed in WebKit May 2021, bug #225875).
      This means nexttrack/previoustrack CAN change audio.src.

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## SESSION CONTROLLER INTEGRATION  (ARCHIVED — SessionController is DELETED)
  ## ==========================================================================

  session_controller_additions:
    status: "VOID — packages/player-vue/src/playback/SessionController.ts no longer exists"
    live_replacement: |
      The whole SessionController/CyclePlayer/PriorityRoundLoader/RoundBuilder
      playback island was deleted. Round/cycle navigation now lives on the
      SimplePlayer class (packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts):
        - roundIndex (state) replaces currentRoundIndex
        - skipRound() / jumpToRound(index, cycleIndex?) replace jumpToPosition()
        - skipToPhase() / next / prev cycle nav also live here
      Round loading is now composables/useInstantPlayback.ts (bootstrap →
      round-map + cycles, localStorage-cached), with INSTANT_PLAYBACK_ALL=true
      in LearningPlayer.vue. The methods below were never added anywhere.
    file: "(none — formerly packages/player-vue/src/playback/SessionController.ts, deleted)"

    new_methods:
      getCyclesForRound:
        signature: "(roundIndex: number) => Cycle[]"
        purpose: "Get all playable cycles for a round (for concatenation)"

      getCyclesForRoundRange:
        signature: "(startRound: number, count: number) => Cycle[]"
        purpose: "Get cycles for multiple rounds (batch concatenation)"

      jumpToPosition:
        signature: "(roundIndex: number, itemIndex: number) => void"
        purpose: "Resume normal mode at specific position"

      getAudioSourceFn:
        signature: "() => GetAudioSourceFn | null"
        purpose: "Expose audio source for driving mode to use"

    new_computed:
      currentRoundIndex: "Expose internal round index"
      totalRounds: "Total number of loaded rounds"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## DATA FLOW  (ARCHIVED — describes the unbuilt concatenator mode)
  ## ==========================================================================

  data_flow:
    enter_driving_mode:
      flow: |
        User taps "Driving Mode" button
          → state = 'preparing'
          → getCyclesForRound(currentRoundIndex)
          → concatenateRound(cycles, getAudioSource)
          → ~2-3 seconds processing
          → mainAudio.src = blobUrl
          → mainAudio.play()
          → setupMediaSession()
          → state = 'playing'
          → Background: concatenate next round

    during_playback:
      flow: |
        mainAudio playing...
          → trackPosition() via requestAnimationFrame
          → Map currentTime to segment
          → Update Media Session position state
          → When timeRemaining < 1s: silentAudio.play()
          → When 'ended': switchToNextRound()

    switch_round:
      flow: |
        mainAudio 'ended' fires
          → silentAudio already playing (session alive)
          → revokeObjectURL(currentRound.blobUrl)
          → mainAudio.src = nextRound.blobUrl
          → mainAudio.play()
          → silentAudio.pause()
          → updateMediaSessionMetadata()
          → Background: concatenate round after next

    exit_driving_mode:
      flow: |
        User taps "Exit" or session complete
          → position = {roundIndex, cycleIndex, phase}
          → cleanup() - stop audio, revoke URLs, clear handlers
          → state = 'inactive'
          → Return position to parent
          → (ARCHIVED) SessionController.jumpToPosition — now SimplePlayer.jumpToRound
          → Normal mode resumes

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## FILES
  ## ==========================================================================

  files:
    archived_never_built:
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/utils/silentAudio.ts"
        purpose: "(DELETED) Generate looped silent WAV blob — the disabled landmine"
        note: "Replaced by playback/silentWav.ts (one-shot data: URI, never looped)"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/utils/audioConcatenator.ts"
        purpose: "(DELETED, 59a17a7b^) Concatenate audio files into single WAV blob"
        note: "Decode/encode core survives in cache/wav.ts for offline playback"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useDrivingMode.ts"
        purpose: "(NEVER CREATED) Main driving mode orchestrator"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/components/DrivingModeToggle.vue"
        purpose: "(NEVER CREATED) UI toggle — there is no separate driving mode"

    live_files_that_deliver_the_goal:
      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/components/LearningPlayer.vue"
        role: "setupMediaSession()/clearMediaSession() (~L4744); owns useAudioSessionKeepalive; hosts SimplePlayer"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/composables/useAudioSessionKeepalive.ts"
        role: "Session-wide silent-oscillator AudioContext holding the iOS audio session alive"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/silentWav.ts"
        role: "buildSilentWavDataUri() — one-shot silent PAUSE clip so locked playback advances on 'ended'"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/playback/SimplePlayer.ts"
        role: "Live cycle/round playback engine; skipRound()/jumpToRound() drive the Media Session handlers"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/cache/wav.ts"
        role: "mp3→16-bit-WAV per-clip decode for offline play (descendant of audioConcatenator)"

      - path: "packages/player-vue/src/components/ListeningOverlay.vue"
        role: "Parallel Media Session + keepalive for Listening-Pod playback"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## QUALITY REQUIREMENTS
  ## ==========================================================================

  quality_requirements:
    must_have:
      - "Background audio continues on iOS Safari when app backgrounded"
      - "Lock screen controls work (play/pause/skip)"
      - "Car bluetooth controls work (steering wheel buttons)"
      - "Seamless round-to-round transitions (< 500ms gap)"
      - "Correct position tracking for resume"
      - "Memory cleanup (no blob URL leaks)"

    should_have:
      - "< 3 second preparation time for first round"
      - "Visual feedback during preparation"
      - "Graceful handling if next round not ready"

    wont_have_v1:
      - "CarPlay integration (requires native app)"
      - "Android Auto integration (requires native app)"
      - "Text display updates while backgrounded"
      - "Playback speed adjustment"

  ## ==========================================================================
  ## TESTING CHECKLIST
  ## ==========================================================================

  testing_checklist:
    ios_safari:
      - "Background audio continues when switching apps"
      - "Background audio continues when locking screen"
      - "Lock screen controls visible and functional"
      - "Round transitions work while backgrounded"
      - "Skip next/previous works from lock screen"
      - "Returning to app shows correct position"

    android_chrome:
      - "Background audio continues"
      - "Notification controls visible"
      - "Bluetooth controls work"

    desktop:
      - "Media keys work (if applicable)"
      - "Tab can be backgrounded"

    edge_cases:
      - "Enter driving mode mid-round"
      - "Exit driving mode mid-cycle"
      - "Last round completes"
      - "Skip when next round not loaded yet"
      - "Low memory conditions"
